Fillets: the walk on from a standing ball's sphere (0670) starts from a
section where the guide's normal planes pass the ball's contacts'
mid-point forwards (mitcad#1428).

A concave groove's rim rounded with 0.5 along a tangent chain that runs
over an earlier convex rounding of 0.5 (the corner between a flange's top
and a slanted side), the slanted side and an earlier rounding of 2 to a
wall square to the groove. Over the corner rounded with 0.5 the ball's
centre stays on that rounding's axis and 0670 makes the rounding a piece
of the ball's sphere; the walk over the slanted side goes on from the
section where the walk's own rule (the contacts' mid-point in the guide's
normal plane) puts that ball, the root of the mid-point's signed distance
from the guide's normal plane nearest to the gap's far end. The guide
turns round the rounding of 2 further on, and its normal plane swings back
through the ball there: a second root, 7.8 along the guide past the right
one (spine parameter 11.66 against 3.86). The walk over the slanted side
started there, its sections' tangents against the guide's, and the stripe
failed as twisted (ChFiDS_TwistedSurface).

- ChFi3d_StandingBallSection takes only the roots where that distance
  decreases along the guide (the normal planes passing the mid-point
  forwards); where it increases the guide turns back past the ball and the
  walk from there would be twisted.

On the design's stored body before the item: the chain rounds, the sphere
piece from spine parameter 2.12 to 3.86, the walked faces on the rolling
ball's envelope within 1e-5 mm and within 0.0013 mm of the stored body's.

